---
source: src/mcp/tools.rs
expression: LIST_PRESETS_DESCRIPTION
---
List available mcp-warden presets — named, scoped actions you may invoke. Returns name, description, type (http|ssh|postgres|mysql|redis), and approval policy (auto|prompt|deny); for SSH presets, also their named commands with what each parameter accepts. Read-only; never returns secret values. Use `proxy_http` for HTTP actions, `ssh_run` for named commands, and `get_secret_for_env` only as a last resort when a child process must read a secret from its environment.
